(D/'DERIVATION.md').write_text("""# Proof frontier and signed decision gain
Let A(r) full legal root actions, I_a=[L_a,U_a] exact intervals, d_a= max(0,max_{b != a} U_b-L_a) in {0,1,2}, D=min_a d_a, W=sum_a(U_a-L_a). D/2 is minimum robust regret upper bound; not the actual chosen action risk unless it minimizes d_a. Both D and W nonincreasing under sound refinements. Root witness iff D=0. For unregistered unknown frontier s, hypothetically assign exact x in {-1,0,1} intersect I(s), not as runtime proof. Recompute every affected ancestor with negamax interval map using overlay J, enqueue all parents after a change. Do not mutate live graph. In topological order the unique interval map under this intervention follows from induction; reverse worklist converges by finite monotone narrowing. Root action intervals use overlay on immediate child even if root value itself does not change. For each hypothetical x define (D-D_x,W-W_x)>=0. Choose lexicographic maximum over x: P(s)=(max primary, max secondary among primary ties). D-D_x divided by2 is possible certified risk reduction from a single hypothetical revelation under relaxation. Values x may be mutually inconsistent with unobserved game rules or shared hidden dependencies; this is optimistic over single-state outcomes, not expected gain, nor an upper bound on arbitrary multi-state actions. Counterexample three independent unknown root actions: revealing one loss/draw leaves D=2 but narrows W; all exact reveals may reduce D=0. If root already certified, additional W decrease has no required WDL value. A resolved node revisited without new descendants has zero new proof information. A frontier path is legal, traverses only currently non-dominated unresolved actions, BFS with exact board identity, at most64 unique frontier states scored; cap is explicit approximate search of candidate set. Each graph state is visited once for path enumeration, multiple parents retained in propagation. Shortest stable BFS path, ties risk then width then shorter path then enumeration order. If maximum pair is (0,0), abstain targeted path. Zero potential does not establish zero future benefit. Revalidate safety at each actual path step, newly solved/dominated child cannot be forced. Potential plan at synchronized block boundary, target up to first two claimed visits, ordinary safe PUCT fallback; actual leaf target hit, forced edges and cost measured, not guarantee full path reaches target (native node unexpanded may stop earlier).
FOCUS: choose top two visited non-dominated materialized root edges by n (tie candidate order). If both visited, |Q1-Q2|<=.25 and challenger unresolved, force challenger for first two claimed visits of block; otherwise fallback. EXPAND: on first two claimed visits, at first expanded node with a hidden eligible unresolved action outside current native width, force first such candidate and widen; rest native selection. Evaluation arm: previous full-child NN blend when |v|<=.65, exact proof overrides; backup arms writer and cross-context-only MERGE as FA04, no blend on proved return or resolved child at read. ACTIVE unresolved-only selection separate control. Safe control includes all exact non-dominated actions, exact leaf skips and root witness. Stop on witness at completed-block boundary for every proof arm; BASE fixed resource. Common prefix32 visits deterministic safe graph with vmode2, B0; BASE standard no graph separate prefix. Retain graph and tree when switching local hooks; ledger begins after prefix.
Signed gain g=U(a_post)-U(a_pre) = R_pre-R_post, can be negative, {-1,-.5,0,.5,1}. Telescoping sum across completed blocks equals final gain. Flip probability times conditional signed delta exact E g=P(flip)E[g|flip]; separate p_gain, p_harm, and cost. Distinguish output-vs-prefix and same-prefix intervention-vs-SAFE effect. For a fixed root policy d, arbitrary approximate recommendation can worsen with more observations (e.g. initially winning move changed to losing). Coherent posterior reoptimization with old decision admissible has nonnegative expected gain but not pathwise. Retention candidate: exact witness always dominates; if pre action remains non-dominated and both pre/post materialized with positive visits, post differs, post visit-share advantage (n_post-n_pre)/N<=threshold, retain pre. This is a heuristic, not guarantee; no oracle access. Train threshold from {.05,.10,.20} vs disabled on actual TRAIN diagnostic final flip pairs, mean gain by source family over proof arms. Require >=6 exposed families, positive mean, otherwise disabled; choose max mean, smallest tie. CAL independent, require >=4 exposed families and nonnegative mean, else disable; no threshold retune. Freeze lock before TEST, output guard and raw from same search; not a live changed continuation policy. No threshold admission from TEST. All pair data clustered by family; report selection exposure and raw/guard gain separately. Resource cost wall+drop and NN count separately; planned equal visits/NN/time targets not actual matched.
""")
